  "body": "### What is the issue with the Cookie Store API Standard?\n\nhttps://github.com/whatwg/cookiestore/commit/ddd94dcf166450837f313946ebce268b564f985e started removing leading and trailing whitespace for _name_ and _value for the set a cookie operation. That seems good as then various checks that happen are aligned with the checks that happen in the network layer.\n\nOne problem is that the delete a cookie operation calls that operation and the delete a cookie operation itself has a length check on _name_. That length check should really happen after leading and trailing whitespace has been removed from _name_ as otherwise we can end up with _name_ and _value both being the empty string which then throws an exception. (I guess I'm okay with the exception as well, but it seems a tad weird.)\n\nAnd then for consistency we should probably trim for the query cookies operation as well so web developers have a uniform API.",
